### Feature ResourceRoles — concesiones rol-recurso (JWT + RBAC)
@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000
# access_token: POST /api/sesion/login (features/auth/session/http/session.http) o npm run dev:token -- admin
@token = pega-aqui-el-access-token

### Listar concesiones activas
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/concesiones-rol
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Concesiones del rol OPERATOR (id 2)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/concesiones-rol?role_id=2
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Obtener concesión
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/concesiones-rol/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Alta en caliente: 1) registrar recurso
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/recursos
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "method": "GET",
  "path": "/api/reportes/ordenes",
  "description": "Reporte de órdenes por cliente"
}

### Alta en caliente: 2) conceder ese recurso a OPERATOR (usa el id devuelto)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/concesiones-rol
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role_id": 2,
  "resource_id": 70
}

### Retirar concesión
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/concesiones-rol/1/deactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Reactivar concesión
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/concesiones-rol/1/reactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ===== Matriz (ISS-CR-02): guardar el estado final de un rol =====
### Usa un rol de prueba (créalo con POST /api/roles), no el único ADMIN real.
### 200 → { message: "Role permissions updated", result: { role_id, activated, deactivated, total_active } }
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/concesiones-rol
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role_id": 3,
  "resource_ids": [1, 2, 3]
}

### Matriz vacía: revoca todas las concesiones activas del rol (200)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/concesiones-rol
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role_id": 3,
  "resource_ids": []
}

### 400: ids duplicados (no cambia nada)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/concesiones-rol
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role_id": 3,
  "resource_ids": [1, 1, 2]
}

### 400: recurso inexistente (no cambia nada)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/concesiones-rol
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role_id": 3,
  "resource_ids": [1, 99999]
}

### 404: rol inexistente o inactivo
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/concesiones-rol
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role_id": 99999,
  "resource_ids": [1]
}
